{
  "text": "The new engineers showed up ready to help. But they had no system access yet, barely knew the product, and had never seen how the architecture fit together. So the senior engineers stepped in, setting up environments, walking through domain rules, reviewing every early change, catching mistakes before they shipped. Delivery slowed even further. But that cost alone didn't make the decision wrong. New people need support before they can contribute, a few difficult months could still buy a real gain later.",
